# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Shell scripts MUST keep LF in the working tree, on every platform. With core.autocrlf=true a
# Windows checkout would otherwise get CRLF, and `sh` reads the trailing \r as part of the command
# -- the error is `$'\r': command not found`, which names the shell rather than the line endings.
# These scripts also run inside containers, where the same file is mounted directly.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Compressed archives are BYTES, and `* text=auto` above must not be allowed to guess at them.
#
# The chart carries the migration chain as one gzip per file (see the header of
# templates/jobs/db-init.yaml). `text=auto` applies git's binary HEURISTIC to those, and a heuristic
# is the wrong instrument here: misclassify one archive of twenty-one and a Windows checkout
# CRLF-normalises it, every 0x0d byte in the deflate stream becomes 0x0d0a, and the file stops
# decompressing. That surfaces at deploy time as db-init failing to gunzip -- which is a database
# with no schema, reported as a dozen unrelated service faults.
#
# `binary` is shorthand for `-text -diff`, so it also stops git printing 149 KiB of deflate noise
# into a diff.
*.gz binary
